Maybe it should be possible to neutralize a curse with a spell. I have always
disliked the spellbooks because they are almost the same as wands and scrolls.
And I have never run out of magic power (did somebody do on this network?)

So, I think there should be major change in spellbooks (does somebody
disagree?). First there should be lots of cursing and blessings that can be
listed by the user.

	Your cursings
		Punishment (the heavy iron ball)
		Losing hitpoints (you lose some hitpoint ones in a while,
				  not max hitpoints!)
		Gain experience block (you can't get experience points 
				       any more)
		Amnesias (you lose parts of your map sometimes)
		Aggravate monster (so this is not an ability any more,
				   are monster aggavated by a smell or
				   a curse?)
		Fumbling
	Your blessings:
		Clairvoyance
		Telepathy (as from a helm of telepathy)
		See cursings and blessing (a Priest starts with this, 
					   difficult to get but also difficult
					   to lose)
		Secret detection (you will see all hidden doors and traps
				  immediatly)

A wizard monster can cast a curse spell (like punishment). However if you
have a spell neutralize punishment spell the game asks you if you want
to neutralize that spell. There is no limit on spells (so many spells
should be removed from the game). If you enter an Opulent throne with many
wizards you should have read many spellbooks to neutralize all different kind
of spells. In any way you will probably run out of magic power (except if you
have very much intelligence).

The only two problems are that is not AD&D and that it is not fair (you can't
punish monsters, however some can punish you).

Any more ideas?

